The utility is provided to allow shell scripts to safely use tem‐
porary  files.   It  creates temporary files or directories using
unique names, and prints the names.  The name of  each  temporary
file  or  directory is derived from a template that includes sev‐
eral trailing characters, such as The trailing characters in  the
template  are  replaced  with a unique letter and number combina‐
tion.  Any characters other than at the end of the  template  are
taken  literally.  The number of unique file names can return de‐
pends on the number of trailing in the template; six will  result
in  testing roughly 62 ** 6 (56800235584) combinations.  The tem‐
plates used to create the unique names are derived from  the  op‐
tion,  or the arguments, possibly modified by other options.  Any
number of temporary files or directories may be created in a sin‐
gle invocation using multiple arguments.  It is possible to spec‐
ify both a option and one or more arguments, but this is not usu‐
ally done.  If neither a option, nor any arguments are specified,
then the default is equivalent to If can successfully generate  a
unique  file name, the file is created with mode 0600 (unless the
flag is given) and the filename is printed  to  standard  output.
